{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"values-known-at-runtime","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Values known at runtime"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kirana compiles styles, but some values are only known when the component runs: a\nprogress width, a colour from data, a variant from props. Those are fine to write\nwhere you write everything else: the compiler classifies each one and picks a\nrepresentation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"three-classes-of-value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Three classes of value"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Known at build time. Compiles to a class. Nothing else happens."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finite dynamic."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A choice between a known set of static values:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"<div sx={css({ color: tone === \"danger\" ? \"crimson\" : \"black\" })} />","lang":"tsx","html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">div</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">color</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">tone</span> === <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;danger&quot;</span> ? <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;crimson&quot;</span> : <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;black&quot;</span> })} /&gt;"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both values are compiled to classes, and the element gets a class "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"expression"}]},{"type":"text","value":", a\nternary between two class strings. Still no CSS at runtime."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open dynamic."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A value the compiler cannot enumerate:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"<div sx={css({ inlineSize: `${percent}%` })} />","lang":"tsx","html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">div</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">inlineSize</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">`</span><span class=\"th-token th-operator\">${</span>percent<span class=\"th-token th-operator\">}</span><span class=\"th-token th-string\">%`</span> })} /&gt;"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The declaration becomes "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"inline-size: <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">var</span>(--k…)","source":"inline-size: var(--k…)"}},{"type":"text","value":", and the element gets that custom\nproperty in its "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"style","source":"style"}},{"type":"text","value":" attribute. One rule, any value, and the browser does the\nrest. The compiler reports it as "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"dynamic-bridged","source":"dynamic-bridged"}},{"type":"text","value":" (informational), so you can see\nwhere runtime values enter your styles."}]},{"type":"component","name":"figure-dynamic","attributes":{},"children":[]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-branch-budget","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The branch budget"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A finite dynamic value with too many branches would multiply classes, so there is\na budget: 16 branches by default, configurable as\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/reference/config","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"dynamic.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">branchBudget</span>","source":"dynamic.branchBudget"}}]},{"type":"text","value":". Past it, the compiler stops and\nreports "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"branch-budget-exceeded","source":"branch-budget-exceeded"}},{"type":"text","value":" rather than emitting a combinatorial explosion.\nUsually that is a sign the value should be a bridge, or a\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/recipes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"recipe"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-ships","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What ships"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A module that needs runtime merging or a bridge imports a private helper that is\nunder 1.1 kB minified and gzipped. It merges class strings and sets custom\nproperties. It never parses styles and never generates CSS."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modules with only static styles import nothing."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-is-not-allowed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What is not allowed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two things the compiler refuses, because they would mean generating styles at\nruntime:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"css({ [key]: value }) // error: dynamic-key\ncss({ ...someObject }) // error: dynamic-spread","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ [key]: value }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// error: dynamic-key</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ ...someObject }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// error: dynamic-spread</span>"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A style built from data is refused too. Some calls only ever build a plain object,\nnever a handle, and a merge cannot apply an object:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-type\">Object</span>.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">fromEntries</span>","source":"Object.fromEntries"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-type\">Object</span>.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">assign</span>","source":"Object.assign"}},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-type\">Object</span>.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">create</span>","source":"Object.create"}},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-type\">JSON</span>.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">parse</span>","source":"JSON.parse"}},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"structuredClone","source":"structuredClone"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passing what one returns to "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>()","source":"css()"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">cx</span>()","source":"cx()"}},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"not-evaluable","source":"not-evaluable"}},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"css(Object.fromEntries(entries)) // error: not-evaluable","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>(<span class=\"th-token th-type\">Object</span>.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">fromEntries</span>(entries)) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// error: not-evaluable</span>"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Write the declarations out instead. A value the compiler cannot read in a handle\nposition is otherwise taken as a handle known at runtime, which is what lets\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>(base, props.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">sx</span>)","source":"css(base, props.sx)"}},{"type":"text","value":" merge a caller's style."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A style's "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"shape"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is fixed at build time; its "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"values"}]},{"type":"text","value":" may vary. If you need a\ndifferent property depending on state, write both and choose between handles:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"<div sx={vertical ? styles.vertical : styles.horizontal} />","lang":"tsx","html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">div</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={vertical ? styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">vertical</span> : styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">horizontal</span>} /&gt;"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keeping-runtime-values-honest","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keeping runtime values honest"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer a finite set when there is one: a class expression costs nothing in the\nbrowser, a bridge costs a custom property."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bridge lengths, colours and numbers: values that vary continuously."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a page reports many "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"dynamic-bridged","source":"dynamic-bridged"}},{"type":"text","value":" values you did not expect, something\nthat could be static is not: usually a token read through an intermediate\nvariable the evaluator cannot follow."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"values-known-at-runtime","text":"Values known at runtime","level":1},{"id":"three-classes-of-value","text":"Three classes of value","level":2},{"id":"the-branch-budget","text":"The branch budget","level":2},{"id":"what-ships","text":"What ships","level":2},{"id":"what-is-not-allowed","text":"What is not allowed","level":2},{"id":"keeping-runtime-values-honest","text":"Keeping runtime values honest","level":2}]}
